        "decision_path": "reports/1851-1855/review/parent-decisions/batch-21.json",
        "decision_sha256": "990d2a962decd38d0c378621f7b25c7335d8490b2de39a25537a1cc4b55acd87",
        "ledger_path": "data/annotations/periods/1851-1855/batch-21.json",
        "ledger_sha256": "043e7a241e053a498d1fcc8639b44466baf72af0403de84b744821e787a326d1",
        "accepted_note": "July 29: Susan forwarded Fox letter addressed to her; Darwin acknowledges third-party communication. Apparatus records death same day, but Darwin still hopes the girl may be spared.",
        "accepted_decision": "dated_grounding_unpaired; third-party and same-day knowledge boundaries.",
        "ledger_requirement": "Preserve receipt/knowledge boundary and third-party authorship."
      },
      "primary_dom_evidence": [
        {
          "letter_id": "DCP-LETT-1526",
          "dom_locator": "/html/body/div[7]/div/div/div/div/div[2]/div/div[3]/div[1]/div/div[1]/div[2]/p[2]",
          "raw_html": "<p>Susan has forwarded your letter to her, here.— What a fearful state you have been, &amp; indeed, I fear, still are in.— I hardly ever heard of anyone having passed through a worse ordeal.<sup id=\"back-mark-Lfoot.f1\" class=\"footnote\" data-target=\"#Lfoot.f1\">1</sup> I am deeply rejoiced that your health has as yet stood it. How earnestly both Emma &amp; I hope that your poor little girl may be spared.—<sup id=\"back-mark-Lfoot.f2\" class=\"footnote\" data-target=\"#Lfoot.f2\">2</sup> I write this chiefly to show that I have heard about you.</p>\n",
          "source_sha256": "fefd85b5091e029258dcee5839af8c35c3ec8a7193d3fb6ecaf190dae684aa06"
        }
      ]
    },
